# DN-49: permanent, shareable "is this real" pages for compliance-module
# certificates (see docs/paid-verifiable-certificates-scoping.md). Must
# stay ABOVE the catch-all "/* -> /index.html" rule below - first match
# wins, so if this were below the catch-all every /verify/<slug> link
# would 200 into the landing page instead of ever reaching
# verify-credential-v2.
#
# Moved here from netlify.toml's [[redirects]] because that second
# [[redirects]] block was silently not being applied in production (only
# the pre-existing catch-all rule ever took effect, confirmed by directly
# curling a fresh /verify/<slug> and seeing the landing page instead of
# the function's output, even after a force=true retry) - an _redirects
# file is the more battle-tested mechanism, so this sidesteps whatever
# was dropping the second netlify.toml rule.
/verify/*  /.netlify/functions/verify-credential-v2/:splat  200
/*  /index.html  200
